Build profiles
==============

The package honours one profile of its own, besides the usual ones:

pkg.oaklisp.disable-readline
	Build the emulator without GNU readline, so that it reads the
	terminal a character at a time with no editing, history or
	completion.  The libreadline-dev build dependency is dropped
	and the build configures --with-readline=no.

	  dpkg-buildpackage -P pkg.oaklisp.disable-readline

	Without the profile the build configures --with-readline=yes.
	Neither way is readline left to configure's own search for the
	library, so a build dependency that is missing on the build
	machine is an error rather than a quietly poorer package.

nodoc
	As usual: the oaklisp-doc package and the LaTeX build
	dependencies are dropped, and the build configures
	--disable-docs.

 -- Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>, Wed,  7 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0100
